  "caption": "Quinn bit into a giant burger and the jaw went CLICK. Now it clicks on every yawn, aches by the afternoon, and long laptop days bring headaches.\n\nJaw pain, clicking and tension headaches often come from overworked jaw muscles or the joint disc, usually with the neck involved. Clenching or grinding at night or during screen work can amplify it. Painless clicking on its own doesn't always need treatment.\n\nWhat can help: a relaxed resting position (teeth apart, tongue on the palate), catching daytime clenching, gentle controlled opening exercises with hands-on care, and looking at sleep, stress and screen habits, working with your dentist.\n\nGet it checked if the jaw locks, opening keeps reducing, or there's trauma, swelling, fever or unexplained tooth pain.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
